# Trivy suppressions — see .github/workflows/ci.yml (`security` + `docker-build` jobs).
# Format: one advisory ID per line; lines starting with # are comments.
#
# Phase 1 (task 4) cleared the previous base-image suppressions: the Dockerfile
# now digest-pins python:3.11-slim AND removes the unused system-Python
# pip/setuptools/wheel from the runtime stage, so CVE-2026-23949,
# GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964, CVE-2025-47273 and CVE-2026-24049 no longer have a
# package to match. A local `trivy image` scan of the rebuilt image is clean.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Legacy Streamlit manifest (requirements.txt) — retained one cycle
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CVE-2026-25087 — Apache Arrow C++ use-after-free DoS via malicious Arrow IPC
# input. Dependabot has since bumped requirements.txt to pyarrow==25.0.1 and a
# local `trivy fs` scan no longer flags it; this line is kept only until CI
# confirms green, and is removed for good in deployment_stages.md Phase 9 when
# requirements.txt is deleted. Not exploitable regardless: the Streamlit app
# reads only its own trusted parquet, and requirements.txt is used by neither
# CI, the API, nor the image.
CVE-2026-25087
